  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training in the Conservation of Ethnographic Objects and Traditional Architecture at Nyamata Church in Bugesera District</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A traditional mud-brick building and today a national genocide memorial, Nyamata was once the largest church in the region, drawing together members of diverse ethnic backgrounds. This project includes training in the conservation of ethnographic objects and traditional architecture for Rwandan stewards.</narrative>
  </description>
